<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arnulfo Arias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1901">1901</a>–<a href="/years/1988">1988</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arnulfo Arias was a Panamanian physician and nationalist politician who was elected President of Panama three times and removed by force each time. His first term brought a new constitution in 1941 and measures against foreign minorities before he was deposed later that year; he was removed again in 1951. Elected in 1968, he was overthrown by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-guard-panama">National Guard</a> after eleven days, opening the military era of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omar-torrijos">Omar Torrijos</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arnulfo-arias.jpg" alt="Arnulfo Arias" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Department of State. U.S. Embassy, Panama. 4/3/1964 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A._Arias_President_of_Panama_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
